WEBVTT

00:00:11.805 --> 00:00:13.390
ALBERTO: Look, we gotta ride together.

00:00:13.473 --> 00:00:15.267
If you don't sit on the back
and hold on to the front,

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.768
the whole thing falls apart.

00:00:16.852 --> 00:00:19.271
Oh. And who's holding the ramp?

00:00:19.646 --> 00:00:22.107
The turtle. Come on.
He's faster than he looks.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.609
Oh, okay. Here we go.

00:00:26.194 --> 00:00:27.737
You, uh, coming?

00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:30.198
Nope. I can't do it.
Never in a million years.

00:00:30.282 --> 00:00:32.117
Hey, hey, hey. I know your problem.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.451
You've got a Bruno in your head.

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:35.161
-A Bruno?
-Yeah.

00:00:35.245 --> 00:00:36.413
I get one, too, sometimes.

00:00:36.496 --> 00:00:38.957
"Alberto, you can't."
"Alberto, you're gonna die."

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.876
"Alberto, don't put that in your mouth."

00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:44.045
Luca, it's simple.
Don't listen to stupid Bruno.

00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:46.631
Why is his name Bruno?

00:00:46.715 --> 00:00:47.716
I don't care. It doesn't matter.

00:00:47.799 --> 00:00:48.884
Call him whatever you want.

00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:51.386
Shut him up. Say, "Silenzio, Bruno."

00:00:54.014 --> 00:00:55.140
Silenzio, Bruno.

00:00:55.223 --> 00:00:57.434
Louder! "Silenzio, Bruno!"

00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:59.644
-Silenzio, Bruno.
-"Silenzio, Bruno!"

00:00:59.728 --> 00:01:00.729
Silenzio, Bruno!

00:01:00.812 --> 00:01:03.315
-Can you still hear him?
-Nope! Just you!

00:01:03.398 --> 00:01:05.483
Good! Now, hang on!

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:07.611
(CLICKS TONGUE)

00:01:07.694 --> 00:01:09.237
Andiamo!

00:01:09.321 --> 00:01:10.739
(LUCA WHIMPERING)

00:01:11.781 --> 00:01:13.200
(ALBERTO WHOOPING)

00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:15.493
-ALBERTO: Yeah!
-(GRUNTS)

00:01:15.577 --> 00:01:17.537
(ALBERTO CONTINUES WHOOPING)

00:01:18.622 --> 00:01:19.998
Silenzio, Bruno. Silenzio, Bruno.

00:01:20.081 --> 00:01:21.082
Silenzio, Bruno.

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:22.876
-Silenzio, Bruno.
-(WHOOPING)

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.921
(DRAMATIC ORCHESTRAL MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:30.717
(SEAGULLS SQUAWKING)

00:01:32.636 --> 00:01:34.554
-Whoa.
-Wow.

00:01:34.638 --> 00:01:35.639
-Uh-oh.
-(WHIMPERS)

00:01:36.139 --> 00:01:37.807
(BOTH YELLING)

00:01:42.938 --> 00:01:44.439
(BOTH GASPING)

00:01:44.523 --> 00:01:46.566
-Whoo-hoo! Yeah!
-(LAUGHS)

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.528
Yes! We're alive! I can't believe it!

00:01:49.611 --> 00:01:51.404
-Take that, Bruno!
-Yes!

00:01:51.488 --> 00:01:52.822
(CRICKETS CHIRPING)

00:01:55.158 --> 00:01:57.410
LUCA: What are all those tiny lights?

00:01:57.744 --> 00:01:59.913
Anchovies. They go there to sleep.

00:02:01.665 --> 00:02:02.874
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:03.041 --> 00:02:05.001
And the big fish protects them.

00:02:05.085 --> 00:02:06.086
I touched it once.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.129
I don't know, it felt like a fish.

00:02:08.213 --> 00:02:09.214
Wow.

00:02:09.297 --> 00:02:11.675
Your life is so much cooler than mine.

00:02:11.758 --> 00:02:13.009
I never go anywhere.

00:02:13.635 --> 00:02:15.262
I just dream about it.

00:02:15.512 --> 00:02:16.680
You came up here.

00:02:16.847 --> 00:02:17.931
Thanks to you.

00:02:18.598 --> 00:02:21.017
Otherwise, I never would've
seen any of this.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.940
Have you ever gone to the human town?

00:02:27.023 --> 00:02:28.024
Yeah!

00:02:28.108 --> 00:02:29.526
Uh... No.

00:02:29.609 --> 00:02:31.945
But, but my dad told me all about it.

00:02:32.028 --> 00:02:33.572
So, I'm pretty much an expert.

00:02:34.573 --> 00:02:36.283
Your dad sounds so cool.

00:02:36.491 --> 00:02:38.368
You're lucky he lets you do what you want.

00:02:38.785 --> 00:02:39.870
Yeah. For sure.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.792
Hey, you remember that time
we almost hit that rock?

00:02:45.876 --> 00:02:47.252
-(LAUGHS)
-And we flew through the air,

00:02:47.335 --> 00:02:50.338
and I was like, "Yeah!"
And then you were like, "No!"

00:02:50.422 --> 00:02:51.423
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:02:52.883 --> 00:02:55.468
Wouldn't it be amazing
to have a real Vespa?

00:02:55.552 --> 00:02:58.555
Yeah. That's the dream.

00:02:59.181 --> 00:03:00.307
Yeah.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.394
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:03:04.477 --> 00:03:06.313
(UPBEAT INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)

00:03:06.396 --> 00:03:07.522
LUCA: Whoo!

00:03:09.149 --> 00:03:10.901
Oh, Luca, look!

00:03:12.068 --> 00:03:13.653
-(ENGINES REVVING)
-BOTH: Whoa!

00:03:13.737 --> 00:03:15.572
-Wild Vespas!
-(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:03:16.406 --> 00:03:17.574
Whoo-hoo!

00:03:18.617 --> 00:03:19.910
Luca, take over!

00:03:21.036 --> 00:03:23.163
(CHUCKLES) Yeah, man!

00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:27.667
Come on, faster!

00:03:27.751 --> 00:03:28.960
(ENGINE REVVING)

00:03:29.044 --> 00:03:32.047
Yeah! Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.508
Whoo-hoo!

00:03:34.591 --> 00:03:36.343
(UPBEAT INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC
CONTINUES)

00:03:37.761 --> 00:03:38.803
(LUCA GASPS)

00:03:42.474 --> 00:03:44.267
BOTH: Whoa.

00:03:45.936 --> 00:03:47.020
(GASPS)

00:03:48.647 --> 00:03:51.191
I'm doing it, Alberto! I'm doing it!

00:03:51.816 --> 00:03:52.817
Alberto?

00:03:53.485 --> 00:03:55.237
(WHIMPERING)

00:03:56.613 --> 00:03:58.073
(YELLING)

00:03:59.783 --> 00:04:02.536
(GASPS) Oh, no! I fell asleep!

00:04:02.702 --> 00:04:03.954
What?

00:04:04.412 --> 00:04:05.789
(SNORING)

00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:08.792
Phew.

00:04:08.875 --> 00:04:10.293
-(DANIELA CLEARS THROAT)
-(GASPS)

00:04:13.755 --> 00:04:14.756
Uh...

00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:18.343
Daniela, do we really need
to go through with this?

00:04:18.426 --> 00:04:19.553
With what?

00:04:19.636 --> 00:04:22.806
Uh, son, you're in big trouble.

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:24.558
You need to promise us

00:04:24.641 --> 00:04:28.311
that you'll never sneak off
to the surface again.

00:04:28.395 --> 00:04:29.980
Uh, I'm really sorry.

00:04:30.063 --> 00:04:33.316
But, you know, it's not
that dangerous up there.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.526
Maybe I could show you.

00:04:34.609 --> 00:04:37.195
I told you. Our son has a death wish.

00:04:37.279 --> 00:04:38.947
But, Mom, we're always careful!

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.031
BOTH: "We"?

00:04:40.991 --> 00:04:43.577
Me and my friend, Alberto.

00:04:43.952 --> 00:04:46.037
But it's okay. He's one of us.

00:04:46.121 --> 00:04:49.833
Ah, yes. There's usually a bad influence.

00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:53.170
Good thing you sent for me
when you did, huh?

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.257
Luca, this is my brother, your Uncle Ugo.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.176
Thanks again for coming all this way

00:04:59.259 --> 00:05:00.552
on such short notice.

00:05:01.428 --> 00:05:02.679
Of course.

00:05:02.762 --> 00:05:03.972
Hello, Luca.

00:05:04.055 --> 00:05:06.600
It's really nice to... (CHOKES)

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.435
(STIFLED WHINING)

00:05:08.518 --> 00:05:10.395
Luca, I need you to punch his heart.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.772
That's right. The red thing. Punch it.

00:05:12.856 --> 00:05:14.274
-Harder!
-Oh.

00:05:14.357 --> 00:05:15.984
-(GRUNTS)
-(UNCLE UGO COUGHING)

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.820
Thanks for that. Too much oxygen up here.

00:05:18.904 --> 00:05:22.532
Not like the deep.
As you'll learn. (LAUGHS)

00:05:23.241 --> 00:05:24.242
What?

00:05:24.326 --> 00:05:25.869
Sure, there's no sunlight,

00:05:25.952 --> 00:05:28.246
but there's nothing to see anyway.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:32.083
Or do. It's just you and your thoughts,

00:05:32.834 --> 00:05:36.046
and all the whale carcass you can eat.

00:05:36.254 --> 00:05:38.965
Little bits of it
just float into your mouth.

00:05:39.049 --> 00:05:40.217
You can't stop it.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.719
You can't see it. So if you...

00:05:42.802 --> 00:05:45.722
The mouth opened,
the whale carcass go in.

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:48.016
Yes, good. I recommend it.

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.519
Come on. No time to waste.

00:05:50.602 --> 00:05:52.354
Mom, what does he mean?

00:05:52.437 --> 00:05:54.397
You're going to stay with Uncle Ugo

00:05:54.481 --> 00:05:55.607
for the rest of the season.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:56.775
No, I can't!

00:05:56.858 --> 00:05:59.361
Two seasons, then. Wanna go for three?

00:05:59.444 --> 00:06:00.820
Why are you doing this?

00:06:00.904 --> 00:06:03.698
The world is a very dangerous place, Luca,

00:06:03.782 --> 00:06:06.201
and if I have to send you
to the bottom of the ocean

00:06:06.284 --> 00:06:07.911
to keep you safe, so be it.

00:06:07.994 --> 00:06:09.287
You don't know what it's like up there!

00:06:09.371 --> 00:06:12.457
I know you. And I know
what's best for you.

00:06:12.541 --> 00:06:14.167
It's done.

00:06:15.627 --> 00:06:18.088
Hey. Look me in the eye.

00:06:18.588 --> 00:06:20.757
You know I love you, right?

00:06:21.174 --> 00:06:22.384
(GRUNTS ANGRILY)

00:06:24.719 --> 00:06:26.179
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:33.311
(GIGGLES)

00:06:34.271 --> 00:06:36.106
LUCA: They're sending me to the deep!

00:06:36.189 --> 00:06:37.816
To live with my weird see-through uncle!

00:06:37.899 --> 00:06:39.484
-What do I do?
-Stay?

00:06:39.568 --> 00:06:41.361
Up here? They'll come looking for me.

00:06:41.444 --> 00:06:42.988
Okay, that may be true,

00:06:43.613 --> 00:06:46.908
but will they come
looking for you over there?

00:06:48.076 --> 00:06:49.828
No way. That's crazy.

00:06:49.911 --> 00:06:52.414
I mean, that place must be full of Vespas.

00:06:52.497 --> 00:06:54.416
-There's gotta be one for us.
-Huh.

00:06:54.541 --> 00:06:56.084
A real Vespa.

00:06:56.459 --> 00:06:58.003
Could we even survive over there?

00:06:58.086 --> 00:07:00.839
You and me? We can do anything.

00:07:00.922 --> 00:07:02.591
We'd swim right over to Vespatown,

00:07:02.674 --> 00:07:03.758
track down Signor Vespa,

00:07:03.842 --> 00:07:05.969
Wait. Do you really think
there's a Signor Vespa?

00:07:06.052 --> 00:07:07.971
-Makes sense, right?
-Yes. Continue.

00:07:08.054 --> 00:07:11.975
And we say, "Signor Vespa,
build us one of these!"

00:07:12.058 --> 00:07:14.853
Whoa. This is the greatest
drawing I've ever seen.

00:07:14.936 --> 00:07:17.731
Yeah, I know. Luca, think about it.

00:07:17.981 --> 00:07:19.900
Every day, we'll ride someplace new,

00:07:19.983 --> 00:07:22.611
and every night,
we'll sleep under the fish.

00:07:22.694 --> 00:07:25.697
No one to tell us what to do.
Just you and me out there.

00:07:26.323 --> 00:07:27.324
Free.

00:07:27.407 --> 00:07:28.491
-ALBERTO: Whoo-hoo!
-(LUCA LAUGHS)

00:07:28.575 --> 00:07:30.452
Take me, gravity!

00:07:32.829 --> 00:07:33.872
(SIGHS)

00:07:34.331 --> 00:07:36.041
(SEAGULLS SQUAWKING IN DISTANCE)

00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:38.376
Silenzio, Bruno.

00:07:39.252 --> 00:07:40.837
Whoo-hoo!

00:07:42.047 --> 00:07:43.131
ALBERTO: Yeah!

00:07:43.798 --> 00:07:44.799
(LUCA LAUGHS)

00:07:44.883 --> 00:07:46.927
(ADVENTUROUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:07:48.094 --> 00:07:49.888
-(GRUNTS)
-(LUCA YELPING)

00:07:51.473 --> 00:07:52.516
(LUCA WHIMPERS)

00:07:53.683 --> 00:07:55.352
ALBERTO: (LAUGHS) Come on!

00:07:56.645 --> 00:07:57.771
Ha-ha!

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.234
(LAUGHS AND GASPS)

